    "### Recommended Database Architecture: PostgreSQL (Primary) + Redis (Caching/Lookups)\n\n#### Why PostgreSQL?\n- **Pragmatic & Versatile**: Battle-tested, free, excellent JSONB support for flexible storage (audit outputs, Wolfram maps, badge data). Handles graphs via recursive CTEs (no extensions needed initially) or Apache AGE (graph extension, optional). Full-text search, UUID/ULID support, ACID transactions.\n- **JSON Lookups**: JSONB with GIN indexes + `@>`/path operators for fast queries (e.g., `audit_outputs @> '{\"flow\": \"success\"}'`).\n- **Graph Queries**: Adjacency lists in JSONB for simple graphs; recursive CTEs for traversals (imports); upgrade to AGE for Cypher-like queries if needed.\n- **Stack Fit**: Native drivers for FastAPI (SQLAlchemy/Tortoise-ORM/asyncpg) and Go (pgx/lib/pq). Deployable on Docker/K8s.\n- **Scalability**: Vertical scale first; Citus/sharding later. Replaces JSON files/SQLite without lock-in.\n- **Cost/Overhead**: Zero licensing; managed options (Supabase/AWS RDS) for prod.\n- **Alternatives Considered**:\n  | DB | Pros | Cons | Why Not Primary |\n  |----|------|------|-----------------|\n  | MongoDB | JSON-native, aggregation graphs | No ACID by default, weaker joins | Less relational structure needed |\n  | Neo4j | Pure graphs | JSON weak, steep curve | Graphs are ~30% of needs |\n  | ArangoDB | Multi-model | Newer, less ecosystem | Postgres covers 90% simpler |\n  | Redis | Fast lookups | No persistence for graphs | Cache only |\n\n- **Redis Add-On** (Optional, Stage 2+): For hot JSON lookups (e.g., ticket ULIDs → audit JSON) and graph caches (serialized traversals). Use RediSearch/JSON module.\n\n#### High-Level Schema (Normalized + JSONB Flex)\nUse ULIDs (via `pg_ulid` ext or `gen_random_uuid()`) as PKs. Namespaces via `tenant_id` or `project_id`.\n\n```sql\n-- Core tables (relational backbone)\nCREATE TABLE tickets (\n    ulid UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),  -- Ticket ULID\n    project_name TEXT NOT NULL,\n    created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW(),\n    ots_stamp BYTEA NULL,  -- Future OTS (binary proof)\n    l2bl4_badge JSONB NULL,  -- Badge issuance {issued: bool, proof: {...}}\n    INDEX idx_project (project_name)\n);\n\nCREATE TABLE lean_modules (  -- Graph nodes\n    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n    ticket_ulid UUID REFERENCES tickets(ulid) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n    module_path TEXT UNIQUE NOT NULL,  -- e.g., \"Mathlib.Data.List.Basic\"\n    src_hash TEXT,  -- Git/commit hash\n    INDEX idx_ticket (ticket_ulid)\n);\n\nCREATE TABLE import_edges (  -- Graph edges\n    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n    src_module UUID REFERENCES lean_modules(id),\n    tgt_module UUID REFERENCES lean_modules(id),  -- tgt = imported by src\n    type TEXT NOT NULL,  -- \"mathlib\", \"external\", \"wolfram\"\n    refs JSONB NULL  -- Mathlib/external details {version: \"v4.5\", url: \"...\"}\n);\n\n-- Flexible blobs\nCREATE TABLE audit_flows (\n    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n    ticket_ulid UUID REFERENCES tickets(ulid) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n    flow_name TEXT NOT NULL,\n    outputs JSONB NOT NULL,  -- Audit results {steps: [...], status: \"pass\"}\n    INDEX idx_outputs_gin USING GIN (outputs)\n);\n\nCREATE TABLE wolfram_maps (  -- Optional Wolfram companion\n    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n    ticket_ulid UUID REFERENCES tickets(ulid) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n    module_path TEXT,\n    mappings JSONB NULL,  -- {lean_func: \"Wolfram[expr]\", synthesized: bool}\n    INDEX idx_maps_gin USING GIN (mappings)\n);\n```\n\n- **Graph Storage**: `lean_modules` (nodes) + `import_edges` (edges). Adjacency via foreign keys.\n- **JSON Lookups**: GIN indexes on JSONB for `?`, `@>`, `||` ops.\n- **Size Est**: 1M modules/edges ~10GB; JSONB compresses well.\n\n#### Graph & JSON Query Examples\n```sql\n-- JSON Lookup: Audit outputs containing \"error\"\nSELECT * FROM audit_flows WHERE outputs @> '{\"errors\": {}}';\n\n-- Graph Traversal: Recursive imports (CTE, no ext needed)\nWITH RECURSIVE import_graph AS (\n  SELECT m1.*, ARRAY[m1.id] as path\n  FROM lean_modules m1 JOIN import_edges e ON m1.id = e.src_module\n  WHERE m1.module_path = 'Mathlib.Init'\n  UNION\n  SELECT m2.*, ig.path || m2.id\n  FROM lean_modules m2\n  JOIN import_edges e ON m2.id = e.tgt_module\n  JOIN import_graph ig ON e.src_module = ig.id\n)\nSELECT * FROM import_graph LIMIT 100;\n\n-- Wolfram Optional: LEFT JOIN, ignore if NULL\nSELECT lm.*, wm.mappings\nFROM lean_modules lm LEFT JOIN wolfram_maps wm ON lm.module_path = wm.module_path;\n```\n\n#### Staged Implementation Plan\n**Total Timeline**: 2-4 weeks for MVP → prod.\n\n| Stage | Focus | DB Changes | Integration | Effort |\n|-------|-------|------------|-------------|--------|\n| **1: MVP (1 week)**<br>JSON-First | Tickets + basic JSON storage. No graphs. | - `tickets`, `audit_flows` tables.<br>- JSONB for everything else (import_graph as `{nodes: [...], edges: [...]}`).<br>- FastAPI: `/audit/{ulid}` → `db.query(outputs)`.<br>- Go: Forum runner → `pgx` inserts. | - FastAPI: SQLAlchemy.<br>- Go: pgx.<br>- Store OTS/badge as JSONB blobs. | Low: Reuse existing routes. Test JSON lookups. |\n| **2: Graph Enable (1 week)**<br>Queries + Redis | Add import graphs. Cache hot paths. | - Add `lean_modules`, `import_edges`, `wolfram_maps`.<br>- GIN indexes.<br>- Redis: `SET ulid:graph <serialized_json>` for traversals. | - FastAPI: GraphQL endpoint (Ariadne/Strawberry) for `/graph/{ulid}?depth=3`.<br>- Go: Populate edges from Lean parser.<br>- Wolfram: Optional upsert to `wolfram_maps` (flag in config). | Med: Write CTE views. Redis via aioredis/pgredis. |\n| **3: Prod Polish (1-2 weeks)**<br>Scale + OTS | OTS stamps, badges, optimizations. | - `pg_ulid` ext for ULIDs.<br>- AGE ext if Cypher needed (`CREATE EXTENSION age;`).<br>- Partitions on `ticket_ulid`.<br>- Full-text on `module_path`. | - FastAPI: Background Celery for OTS stamping.<br>- Go: Async flow → DB triggers.<br>- Monitoring: pgBadger/Prometheus.<br>- Backup: pg_dump + S3. | Med: Load test 10k tickets. |\n\n#### Deployment Snippet (Docker Compose)\n```yaml\nservices:\n  postgres:\n    image: pgvector/pgvector:pg16  # JSONB + vector bonus if needed\n    env: POSTGRES_DB=lean_automata\n  redis: image: redis:alpine\n  fastapi: build: . ports: [\"8000:80\"]\n  go-runner: build: ./go volumes: [\"/data\"]\n```\n\n#### Risks & Next Steps\n- **Risks**: Graph explosion → Limit depth in queries. Wolfram opt-in via env var `WOLFRAM_ENABLED=false`.\n- **Migration**: From current (JSON?/in-mem) → `pg_dump` scripts.\n- **Next**: Prototype Stage 1 schema in Supabase (free tier). Share DDL for review.\n\nThis is lean, evolvable, and matches your stack—no Wolfram lock-in. Ping for schema SQL or code stubs!",
    "**Recommended Architecture: PostgreSQL + Lightweight Graph Layer**\n\n### Core Principles\n- **Single primary store** for pragmatism (FastAPI + Go ecosystem maturity, operational simplicity, ACID guarantees).\n- **JSONB-first design** for the experimental/fluid parts (Wolfram maps, audit outputs, badge metadata, OTS stamps).\n- **Relational backbone** for tickets, badges, and audit flows (ULID primary keys).\n- **Graph modeled as adjacency list + recursive CTEs/materialized views** — sufficient for Lean import graphs and reference graphs. Only add a dedicated graph DB if query patterns become Cypher-heavy.\n- **Wolfram `LLMSynthesize` kept strictly optional** — nullable column + feature flag.\n\nThis gives you immediate **JSON lookups** (`@>`, `->>`, GIN indexes) and **graph queries** (recursive CTEs, `ltree` for hierarchical imports if desired) without introducing new runtime dependencies in Stage 1.\n\n### Database Schema (Pragmatic Design)\n\n```sql\n-- Core ULID generator (install ulid extension or use app-level)\nCREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS ulid;\n\n-- 1. Tickets & Audit Flows\nCREATE TABLE tickets (\n    ulid        ULID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_ulid(),\n    created_at  TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),\n    updated_at  TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),\n    title       TEXT,\n    status      TEXT,\n    metadata    JSONB NOT NULL DEFAULT '{}',           -- forum data, tags, etc.\n    CONSTRAINT valid_status CHECK (status IN ('open','in_progress','closed',...))\n);\n\nCREATE TABLE audit_flows (\n    ulid          ULID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_ulid(),\n    ticket_ulid   ULID REFERENCES tickets(ulid),\n    runner        TEXT NOT NULL,                       -- 'fastapi' or 'go-forum'\n    route         TEXT,\n    input_hash    TEXT,\n    output        JSONB NOT NULL,                      -- full audit output\n    executed_at   TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),\n    duration_ms   INTEGER,\n    metadata      JSONB NOT NULL DEFAULT '{}'\n);\n\n-- GIN for fast JSON lookups\nCREATE INDEX idx_audit_output_gin ON audit_flows USING GIN (output);\nCREATE INDEX idx_ticket_meta_gin ON tickets USING GIN (metadata);\n\n-- 2. L2BL4 Badges + Future OTS Stamps\nCREATE TABLE badge_issuances (\n    ulid            ULID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_ulid(),\n    ticket_ulid     ULID REFERENCES tickets(ulid),\n    recipient       TEXT NOT NULL,                     -- user/discord/eth address\n    badge_type      TEXT NOT NULL,                     -- 'l2bl4-level1', ...\n    issued_at       TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),\n    metadata        JSONB NOT NULL DEFAULT '{}',       -- criteria, evidence\n    ots_stamp       TEXT,                               -- OpenTimestamps proof (future)\n    blockchain_tx   TEXT,                               -- future L2 tx hash\n    expires_at      TIMESTAMPTZ\n);\n\nCREATE INDEX idx_badge_recipient ON badge_issuances(recipient);\nCREATE INDEX idx_badge_ots ON badge_issuances(ots_stamp) WHERE ots_stamp IS NOT NULL;\n\n-- 3. Lean Source Import Graph (adjacency list)\nCREATE TABLE lean_files (\n    path        TEXT PRIMARY KEY,                      -- normalized path as ID\n    hash        TEXT,\n    last_parsed TIMESTAMPTZ,\n    meta        JSONB NOT NULL DEFAULT '{}'             -- file-level metadata\n);\n\nCREATE TABLE import_edges (\n    source      TEXT REFERENCES lean_files(path),\n    target      TEXT REFERENCES lean_files(path),\n    edge_type   TEXT NOT NULL,                         -- 'import', 'export', 'axiom'\n    is_mathlib  BOOLEAN DEFAULT false,\n    metadata    JSONB NOT NULL DEFAULT '{}',\n    PRIMARY KEY (source, target, edge_type)\n);\n\nCREATE INDEX idx_import_target ON import_edges(target);\nCREATE INDEX idx_import_mathlib ON import_edges(is_mathlib);\n\n-- 4. Wolfram Companion Maps + Mathlib/External References\nCREATE TABLE wolfram_companions (\n    lean_id         TEXT NOT NULL,                     -- theorem/definition key\n    wolfram_id      TEXT,\n    map_type        TEXT NOT NULL,                     -- 'isomorphism', 'analog', ...\n    confidence      NUMERIC(3,2),\n    metadata        JSONB NOT NULL DEFAULT '{}',\n    llm_synthesis   TEXT,                              -- ← NULL by default (optional)\n    synthesized_at  TIMESTAMPTZ,\n    PRIMARY KEY (lean_id, wolfram_id)\n);\n\n-- Optional synthesis flag\nALTER TABLE wolfram_companions ADD COLUMN synthesis_enabled BOOLEAN DEFAULT false;\n\nCREATE TABLE external_references (\n    lean_id      TEXT NOT NULL,\n    target_type  TEXT NOT NULL,                        -- 'mathlib', 'arxiv', 'wikipedia'\n    target_id    TEXT NOT NULL,\n    reference_data JSONB NOT NULL DEFAULT '{}',\n    PRIMARY KEY (lean_id, target_type, target_id)\n);\n\n-- Materialized view for common graph queries\nCREATE MATERIALIZED VIEW mv_transitive_imports AS\nWITH RECURSIVE transitive AS (\n    SELECT source, target, ARRAY[source] AS path, 1 AS depth\n    FROM import_edges\n    UNION ALL\n    SELECT t.source, e.target, t.path || e.target, t.depth + 1\n    FROM transitive t\n    JOIN import_edges e ON t.target = e.source\n)\nSELECT * FROM transitive;\n```\n\n### Staged Implementation Plan\n\n**Stage 1 – Foundation (1–2 weeks)**\n- Core tables: `tickets`, `audit_flows`, `badge_issuances`\n- ULID generation (Python `ulid-py`, Go `oklog/ulid`)\n- FastAPI routes write audit outputs directly (`output` JSONB)\n- Go forum runner writes via `pgx` or HTTP to FastAPI\n- Heavy GIN indexing on JSON fields for lookups (`ticket.metadata @> '{\"forum_id\": 123}'`)\n- Basic OTS column ready for future stamping service\n\n**Stage 2 – Graph + Maps (2–3 weeks)**\n- Add `lean_files`, `import_edges`, `wolfram_companions`, `external_references`\n- Implement common graph queries as Postgres functions:\n  ```sql\n  CREATE FUNCTION get_transitive_imports(root_path TEXT)\n  RETURNS TABLE(source TEXT, target TEXT, depth INT) ...\n  ```\n- Python `asyncpg` + SQLAlchemy 2.0 (or raw SQL for complex CTEs)\n- Go side uses simple query wrappers